{"views": [45, 135, 225, 315], "categories": [{"key": "mining", "label": "Tin and copper", "spots": [24, 18, 23, 22, 13, 12, 11]}, {"key": "bolster", "label": "The giant Bolster", "spots": [16, 17, 19]}, {"key": "village", "label": "The village", "spots": [0, 25, 3, 1, 4, 2]}, {"key": "coast", "label": "Coast and Beacon", "spots": [10, 18, 21, 16, 19, 14, 20]}, {"key": "pubs", "label": "Pubs and cafes", "spots": [6, 8, 9, 7, 5, 15]}, {"key": "gone", "label": "Gone", "spots": [18, 27, 26]}], "spots": [{"name": "St Agnes Parish Church", "note": "A chapel of ease of about 1482, restored in 1848; the spire was rebuilt in 1905", "kind": "Parish church · about 1482", "text": "The church of St Agnes stands in Churchtown, the oldest part of the village. It was built about 1482 as a chapel of ease, and St Agnes became a parish of its own only in 1846. Piers St Aubyn restored the building in 1848, all but the tower and spire; the spire was rebuilt in 1905. A spire is a rare thing on a Cornish church, and this one shows from the Beacon and from the sea.", "x": 172029.5, "y": 50735.4, "poly": [[[371.4, 254.92], [373.67, 251.97], [375.83, 251.28], [377.42, 250.78], [383.94, 250.52], [396.26, 260.19], [396.26, 265.44], [395.61, 269.76], [392.41, 272.19], [376.82, 276.01], [371.4, 260.88]], [[-379.33, 270.17], [-376.48, 267.27], [-358.3, 261.47], [-352.39, 262.6], [-350.02, 264.48], [-349.39, 265.97], [-349.39, 278.1], [-352.57, 288.14], [-377.04, 279.87], [-379.33, 276.34]], [[-396.26, -108.65], [-395.61, -111.74], [-388.8, -113.9], [-383.0, -112.47], [-371.4, -103.38], [-371.4, -97.42], [-373.65, -86.6], [-376.82, -76.56], [-396.26, -103.4]], [[349.39, -111.55], [349.51, -116.2], [368.84, -122.36], [375.01, -122.03], [377.04, -120.44], [379.33, -118.63], [379.33, -112.46], [352.57, -88.68], [349.39, -99.43]]]}, {"name": "St Agnes Methodist Church", "kind": "Methodist church", "text": "The Methodist church of the village, on British Road. Methodism ran deep in the mining district