rnish Mining World Heritage Site.", "more": "https://www.nationaltrust.org.uk/visit/cornwall/wheal-coates", "x": 169878.5, "y": 50011.0, "poly": [[[-629.15, -784.18], [-624.41, -787.19], [-619.27, -785.19], [-618.93, -782.39], [-619.27, -773.05], [-619.49, -768.93], [-619.58, -768.64], [-619.99, -768.44], [-620.56, -768.39], [-621.07, -768.53], [-624.35, -770.79], [-629.15, -775.37]], [[1663.28, -260.22], [1663.53, -262.58], [1667.56, -264.97], [1673.58, -262.6], [1673.58, -253.14], [1669.59, -247.89], [1665.42, -246.35], [1664.91, -246.22], [1664.34, -246.27], [1663.93, -246.47], [1663.84, -246.75], [1663.53, -251.2]], [[618.93, 882.6], [619.08, 882.14], [619.73, 881.82], [624.35, 881.37], [629.15, 883.38], [629.15, 892.2], [624.41, 895.85], [619.27, 896.55]], [[-1673.58, 361.81], [-1669.59, 359.24], [-1665.0, 359.57], [-1664.08, 359.64], [-1663.42, 359.97], [-1663.28, 360.43], [-1663.53, 373.16], [-1663.84, 373.81], [-1664.1, 374.06], [-1664.62, 374.19], [-1665.18, 374.15], [-1673.58, 371.27]]]}, {"name": "Whim Engine House, Wheal Coates", "kind": "Mine engine house", "text": "Up the slope from Towanroath stand the other buildings of Wheal Coates: the whim engine house, whose engine wound the ore up the shaft, the stamps engine house, which crushed it, and the calciner, where the tin ore was roasted to drive off arsenic.", "more": "https://www.nationaltrust.org.uk/visit/cornwall/wheal-coates", "x": 169966.6, "y": 50037.3, "poly": [[[-585.12, -715.88], [-580.22, -717.42], [-574.73, -713.07], [-574.73, -701.01], [-579.64, -700.32], [-584.07, -702.78], [-584.32, -703.02], [-585.12, -706.82]], [[1582.63, -210.03], [1591.33, -212.77], [1594.42, -210.33], [1594.42, -200.41], [1592.92, -198.72], [1592.68, -198.48], [1585.72, -195.51], [1582.63, -198.83]], [[574.73, 872.65], [579.64, 871.1], [585.12, 875.45], [585.12, 884.51], [584.32, 888.91], [584.23, 889.18], [583.85, 889.36], [583.33, 889.41], [582.85, 889.28], [574.73, 884.71]], [[-1594.42, 369.9], [-1585.72, 367.15]